<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Icfb28486a2d72f24213176df7abee900140862da" commit="4ec695267a1e6c42302460f92125f930fadbaa99" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/rockchip: cdn-dp: do not read edid many times  The EDID reading will be called in cdn_dp_connector_get_modes, this function can be called by DRM API, even though the cdn_dp is inactived. At this case, cdn_dp_get_edid_block will cause system crash, since the mailbox of cdn_dp is not ready. Actually, we do not need read the EDID many times, the EDID will not changed, so read it one time after sink connected is enough.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52872 TEST=connect a DP monitor, use ctrl + alt + F2 switch to console mode, modetest, system will not crash  Change-Id: Icfb28486a2d72f24213176df7abee900140862da Signed-off-by: Chris Zhong &lt;zyw@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/397078 Commit-Ready: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="397078" owner_email="zyw@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/78/397078/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I1c7293eea949ea6b28bd368988d7fd789c1e07f0" commit="aece5f10b2664d105df69c0a06bd75f4446dcdb2" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/rockchip: cdn-dp: set default bpc to 8  According to the DP compliance spec, every DP sink must support 8bpc, but 10bpc is not mandatory, so let's change the default bpc to 8 for better compliance.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52872 TEST=Check DP display in some old monitor  Change-Id: I1c7293eea949ea6b28bd368988d7fd789c1e07f0 Signed-off-by: Chris Zhong &lt;zyw@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/397079 Commit-Ready: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="397079" owner_email="zyw@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/79/397079/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I68c294d5dbda7963584923ceb2132b0f2e462e4a" commit="d84dc98cbb0cc733e92603f02fed1329471e08af" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/rockchip: cdn-dp: remove warning log  We add a WARN in event_work to catch a accident IRQ, if only focus one port, we could not get this WARN at anytime, but RK3399 support 2 Type-C ports, if the DP is connected with one port, plug/unplug the USB into the other port will let work meet this condition, so remove this WARN log.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52872 TEST=connect a DP to main port, plug/unplug usb to sub port, no any warning message  Change-Id: I68c294d5dbda7963584923ceb2132b0f2e462e4a Signed-off-by: Chris Zhong &lt;zyw@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/397920 Commit-Ready: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="397920" owner_email="zyw@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/397920/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I37cf4c998856db2d297356776752643dba46a8f8" commit="66bb2a87fcb134e05436469dcd4a4bb47994cd88" commit_message="UPSTREAM: x60,t60: do not add etc/ps2-keyboard-spinup for non-seabios payloads  Regardless of the payload chosen a file etc/ps2-keyboard-spinup is added to cbfs. With this fix this file is only added to cbfs when seabios is choses as a payload.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=None  Signed-off-by: Arthur Heymans &lt;arthur@aheymans.xyz&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/16146 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Alexander Couzens &lt;lynxis@fe80.eu&gt;  Change-Id: I37cf4c998856db2d297356776752643dba46a8f8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/398622 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="398622" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/22/398622/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Idd1363e1abe98ba51c795879db061cc54808da8e" commit="6b607f7967a7c905f1977fdc78fa857ef05f9a38" commit_message="UPSTREAM: coreinfo: make the CBFS list scrollable  This enables viewing more than ~20 files in the file list on the left. Arrows are added to indicate that more items are available off-screen. This mimics what was done in pci_module.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=None  Signed-off-by: Ben Gardner &lt;gardner.ben@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/14546 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Jonathan Neuschfer &lt;j.neuschaefer@gmx.net&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Menzel &lt;paulepanter@users.sourceforge.net&gt; Reviewed-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: Idd1363e1abe98ba51c795879db061cc54808da8e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/398623 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="398623" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count=